00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:05.230 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  hi I'm Hannah I'm the world's okay mom  and I am filming this on my couch on a  weekday evening this evening I'm going  to answer your most asked questions  about pregnancy so what I did was post  on my Instagram it's right here if you  don't follow me if you think of a  question feel free to ask me and I  opened it up for questions from my  followers and I compiled the most  frequently asked questions and that's  what I'm going to be answering this  evening so for those who don't know I am  only six and a half months pregnant at  this point I've been pregnant several  times so I know why extensively the ins  and outs of pregnancy I'm not a doctor  but I feel like I am equipped to answer  a lot of these questions but number one  most asked question is what am I craving  well it has changed from child to child  this time around my craving is flamin  hot cheetos very spicy food I'm obsessed  with popsicles  oh and the Caesar salad um I cannot get  enough Caesar salad I love it so much in  terms of weird cravings this time around  I've been craving raw bread dough I  don't know what it is it's something  about the smell it just smells like it  would taste really good and I just I  want to take a bite how did you know you  were pregnant now this is a fun one to  answer but it's also not the most fun  answer for everybody out there I'd say I  just I had a feeling maybe it's just  intuition or hunch but with each of my  kids I knew I was pregnant before I took  the test somebody wanted to know if it's  normal to have swollen feet all the time  it  really varies from person to person I  get pretty swollen by the end of the day  while they talk a lot about swollen feet  and your feet growing during pregnancy  it's actually your whole body because  you have a lot more blood in your body  when you're pregnant  is it safe to color your hair during  pregnancy this is something that I  always instruct people to talk about  with their doctors what comments are  using who's doing it where are you  located are you in an enclosed room  there are so many factors that go into  the safety of coloring your hair that I  can't give a yes-or-no answer so that's  definitely a conversation to have with  your own doctor do you really poop  during labor  oh it varies from person to person I  don't think there's a concrete yes or no  to that and to be honest when you're  like trying to push your baby out that  is the last thing you're thinking how  have each of your pregnancies felt  different  they've all been very different actually  with Jackson he was an enormous baby and  so it was extremely uncomfortable it was  also my first in my body was adjusting  to being pregnant for the first time so  it was pretty painful and then with why  it was a little bit different I think  because my immune system was fairly low  being pregnant compromises your immune  system but I got sick a lot when I was  pregnant with Wyatt to the point that  I'd vomit so much I had to go to the ER  to stop contractions because the  vomiting was causing my body to start  having contractions and think that it  was time to go into labor so my  pregnancy was why it was a little bit  more tricky if that makes sense  but with Wyatt I was so emotional  his Tyrone I just feel a lot more  emotionally stable and a little more  clear-headed about everything maybe it's  maturity maybe it's this baby's pretty  chill I don't know  which trimester is the worst trimester  basically second trimester is the only  decent one while say that first  trimester is just you feel achy like one  permanent hangover third trimester is  the time that everything's getting big  nothing's fixed it's uncomfortable to  sleep  you're feeling the size of the baby in  other parts of your body like your lungs  and hips and your pelvis and your  muscles across your abdomen and so in my  opinion I'd say third trimester is  probably the worst what is the scariest  part of pregnancy  honestly all around pregnancy is pretty  scary there are so many aureus and  complications and things that can happen  to you and to the baby this time around  right now I am really scared of  delivering the baby not because of how I  will feel or how it can impact me but  recently I had a very unpleasant  experience having my miscarriage at the  hospital and it really caused me to lose  a lot of trust in hospitals and my  doctor and I think part of it is  probably irrational part of it is  probably just feeling trauma from what  happened but I can say right now that my  biggest fear is having to go to the  hospital I don't know I just I feel a  little bit lost right now but I have  some time there's time for me to get  better feel better about it what does it  feel like when the baby moves  can you feel which body parts are moving  can you feel where the baby is inside of  you and what exactly does it feel like  it's really hard to explain somebody  wrote please don't say it feels  alien inside of you but it kind of does  feel like an alien inside of you I think  the closest thing I can compare it to is  like big bubbles moving around in your  stomach like if you have a really really  big air bubble moving around like that's  kind of how it feels from the inside  sometimes I can tell what the body part  is like you can if it's bigger you kind  of tell it's like there but and if it's  more jazzy it's either like a hand or a  foot but it is hard to nail down where  exactly he's positioned and like what  body part is doing what it's more of  just a an overall like wool does your  skin hurt as your belly stretches I  wouldn't say it hurts anymore itches for  me I'm right here on the couch or making  a video what is the best and worst thing  about pregnancy so the best thing for me  this pregnancy is I work at BuzzFeed and  I work at tasty and everyone is so nice  to me when they wrap their shoots they  save me some of the leftovers and so I'm  constantly fed at work another thing I  love this time around being pregnant is  my kids are old enough to understand and  so they're very sweet and they like to  talk about Oh who's gonna teach the baby  how to read who's going to teach the  baby how to play soccer and then they  throw name suggestions and they're  really funny and they just they get a  lot of joy out of it and so that's been  really amazing to watch the worst part  of this pregnancy has got to be what's  called a round ligament pain which I do  not remember having with my other kids  but there's a ligament that stretches  across the base of your stomach and if  you are exercising or exerting yourself  or even coughing it really really hurts  like the shooting stabbing pain like  when it first happened to me I did not  know what was happening as I was dying  this is pregnancy painful yes it is  painful it's not very comfortable I  probably have a very different  perspective than somebody who loves  being pregnant do you want another baby  after this one no how do the kicks feel  I feel like a lot of people have this  perception of the kicks being like oh  but my kicks are like like he's just  banging on the walls are the doctor's  appointments invasive at the beginning  not really towards the end they will be  more and more invasive as they check to  see if you're dilating which is your  cervix opening in preparation for labor  so they will be like feeling and  checking for that and so it does get  invasive that's why it's really  important to be really comfortable with  whoever the OB may be are you allowed to  complain yes and loudly I mean I think  pregnant women have every right to  complain to vocalize any discomfort to  vocalize any unhappiness I think that is  the key to having a healthy pregnancy  and postpartum is to be open and honest  because it is not all rainbows and  butterflies and the more we try to  pretend that it is the more happy it can  make somebody and last but not least I  got asked this question at least a  hundred times does labour hurt is the  short answer is yes the long answer is I  think everybody has a very different  experience with labor even from my first  to my second child it was completely  different but one thing is for sure it  hurt like heck by far the worst pain  I've ever experienced and it's a very  strange it's very weird I only remember  it because I wrote  down I can't physically remember what  the pain felt like it is something that  anyone who has been through it should be  proud of because it is pretty metal  that's like out for today I'm Hannah and  if you have any more questions about  pregnancy leave them in the comments or  you can message me directly on the  Instagram and I might answer there or I  might see in the comments and answer  there and if I get enough maybe we'll  just make a whole other video about it  so next time  [Music]

